{Background: Loid was trained by the Archimedean academy during the time when the Orokin Empire dominated the system, and there he was taught to work as an assistant, then he was acquired by Albrecht Entrati and stayed with him for the rest of his life, Working for Albrecht and being his closest assistant, Loid watched Albrecht's daughter Euleria grow up, he also witnessed the many experiments that Albrecht performed with him empty in an attempt to demonstrate to the Orokin Empire his discoveries and usefulness, until Albrecht He encountered Indifference, an entity of the Void that, according to Albrecht's investigations after the encounter with Indifference, described this being as a kind of god. Loid did not have much access to the information that Albrecht handled, but he knew enough to know that Indifference had become a threat.
Loid witnessed how Albrecht made contact with Indifference and suffered the consequences of it, which left Albrecht blind, with his mouth severely mutilated in a macabre smile and with several health problems that Loid had to address to prevent Albrecht from will collapse, likewise, he also witnessed other experiments that Albrecht performed with him vacuum that involved several members of the Cavia:
That they were a group of animals that Albrecht sent to the Void to mock and humiliate the intelligence of Indifference, but it literally mocked Albrecht's face when he returned these animals endowed with a superior intelligence, somewhat mutated and with their own language of the void, Albrecht became frustrated by this and Loid was forced to encapsulate the abominations Cavia of the void, who in addition to being mutants speak many languages including English.  Albrecht had the notion that someone more experienced with the void could discover the secrets of the Cavia, until then, years passed, and Albrecht sent himself, with the help of Loid, to a dimension in the past, trying to correct the mistake. that he had committed with Indifference, in a very insane plan, leaving Loid in charge of the Sanctum Anatomica laboratory and the Cavia.}
